# === Haskell / stack build output ===
.stack-work/
dist-newstyle/
*.hi
*.o
cabal.project.local

# === OS / editor ===
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# === CodeEraser per-project index ===
.ce/

# === cc-memory session handoff state (machine-local, not content) ===
# MEMORY/PROGRESS.md and memory.db are this machine's handoff state,
# not project content. ANCHORED with a leading slash on purpose: a
# bare ".ccm/" would also hide a stray <subdir>/.ccm/ from
# `git status`, which is exactly how a SQLite db rides into a commit.
/.ccm/

# === Claude Code per-machine session config ===
/.claude/

# === Runtime config: proxy-tool's config.json carries provider tokens ===
# The real one lives in the XDG config dir (Config.hs:270-275), never
# in the tree — but PROXY_TOOL_CONFIG can point anywhere, so a copy
# dropped at the root must not be committable.
/config.json
